{#- The whole manual as one Markdown file.

    One front matter block for the project rather than one per document: front
    matter is only front matter at the top of a file, and a reader that splits
    on "---" would otherwise cut the content into pieces at every heading.

    Documents are separated by a horizontal rule so that a tool which chunks the
    file has a boundary to cut on, and so that a human scrolling through it can
    see where one page ends. -#}
{%- set frontMatter -%}
{%- if project.title %}title: {{ project.title|md_yaml|raw }}
{% endif -%}
{%- if project.version %}version: {{ project.version|md_yaml|raw }}
{% endif -%}
{%- if project.release %}release: {{ project.release|md_yaml|raw }}
{% endif -%}
{%- if project.copyright %}copyright: {{ project.copyright|md_yaml|raw }}
{% endif -%}
{%- if project.lastRendered %}modified: {{ project.lastRendered|date("Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP")|md_yaml|raw }}
{% endif -%}
single-file: true
{%- endset -%}
{%- if frontMatter|trim -%}
---
{{ frontMatter|trim|raw }}
---
{{ "\n" }}{% endif -%}
{#- The sitemap is left out: its page tree is assembled by "sitemap.html",
    which Markdown does not use, so it would contribute a heading with nothing
    under it -- and a list of every page is what this file already is.

    "written" rather than "loop.first" decides where a separator goes: the
    first document may be one of the skipped ones, and the file must not open
    with a horizontal rule. -#}
{%- set written = false -%}
{%- for document in documents -%}
{%- if not isSitemap(document) -%}
{%- set body = renderNode(document)|trim -%}
{%- if body -%}
{%- if written %}{{ "\n" }}---{{ "\n\n" }}{% endif -%}
{{- body|raw -}}
{{ "\n" }}
{%- set written = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
